[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3327174665","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110845#issuecomment-3327174665","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110845","id":3327174665,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GUKgJ","user":{"login":"nestorac","id":26766197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzY2MTk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26766197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nestorac","html_url":"https://github.com/nestorac","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nestorac/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nestorac/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nestorac/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nestorac/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nestorac/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nestorac/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nestorac/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nestorac/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nestorac/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-24T08:24:03Z","updated_at":"2025-09-24T08:24:03Z","body":"I can confirm the problem. Godot 4.5.stable.official on Linux Mint 21.3, Intel i7 8550, Intel UHD620.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3327174665/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3333553484","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110845#issuecomment-3333553484","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110845","id":3333553484,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Gsf1M","user":{"login":"RoyBerardo","id":32561682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTYxNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32561682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo","html_url":"https://github.com/RoyBerardo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-25T11:43:26Z","updated_at":"2025-09-25T11:43:26Z","body":"Just tried out the MRP on 4.6 commit `6e4e8072` (latest as of writing this).\nIt looks like `thunder_close.tres` doesn't have any streams set in it, meaning it plays silence when close thunder is chosen.\n\n<img width=\"479\" height=\"392\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aa4c6fff-fc29-4894-81c2-f902cc997acf\" />`\n\nMaking it only pick distant thunder plays sound every time. I believe everything is working as expected.\n\nThis does bring up a good point, though, that playing an empty `AudioStreamRandomizer` will not immediately stop the `AudioStreamPlayer`. Similar `AudioStream` types that take sub-streams stop immediately when empty, except `AudioStreamPolyphonic` (which I feel is the correct behavior for `AudioStreamPolyphonic`)\n\nPerhaps it'd be worth it to open a new issue highlighting this behavior with the randomizer? I couldn't find any mentioning this. \n\nThis was a very nice thing to debug :) listening to the moody distant thunder with some music on made for a nice experience","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3333553484/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3335660646","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110845#issuecomment-3335660646","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110845","id":3335660646,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7G0iRm","user":{"login":"mrtripie","id":65431647,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NDMxNjQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65431647?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrtripie","html_url":"https://github.com/mrtripie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrtripie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrtripie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrtripie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrtripie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrtripie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrtripie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrtripie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrtripie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrtripie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-25T19:33:48Z","updated_at":"2025-09-25T19:33:48Z","body":"Hmm, it is empty now, and filling in the clips fixed it. I checked several times both randomizers to check if they had any missing steams and I definitely remember it having 3 clips. It also like thunder distant should have had Random Pitch and Random Volume Offset dB set. I'm thinking there might have been an issue somewhere with saving that resource, as it seems that in the resource that was loaded in the editor it was set, but it wasn't saved to disk so when I played the game the resource was empty. I haven't really had a problem before with Godot not automatically saving resources when saving scenes/playing the game, but I usually try to remember to do it manually just in case. I wonder if the file got corrupted and got reset to the default properties since I'm pretty sure I duplicated the resource so as to not have to set the random pitch and volume again, so it should have had something saved when it was duplicated.\n\nOther than that, I agree, I think that AudioStreamRandomizer should stop playing immediately if its empty, and push an error","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3335660646/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]